; claude: a 3D physics engine, from scratch, for teaching, beside
; physics/2d/ and in the same spirit: one idea per module, each .mli
; with its diagram, its worked example and its references (see
; docs/claude_notes/plans/plan_physics3d_teaching.md and
; notes_3d_physics.md). Independent of the Playground -- it knows
; vectors, quaternions, bodies and time steps, and nothing of shape3d,
; camera or computer. In the package tiny_libs, as tiny_libs.physics_3d:
; pure OCaml, so the web backend has it too.
;
; Units are metres and seconds (physics/2d works in pixels), so that a
; 27 mm pinball and a gravity of 9.8 can be written down as themselves.
(library
 (name physics_3d)
 (public_name tiny_libs.physics_3d)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries graphics_3d_geometry) ; Vec3, shared with the renderers
)
